We need to express that after set, elements after index up to size-1 are unchanged (including null). The initial size is before operation, i.e., \old(this.size()).

We also need premise: index >=0 && index < \old(this.size()).

Then for all int i; index < i && i < this.size(); the element at i after operation equals the old element at i. Since after set, size may stay same (set doesn't change size). So this.size() == \old(this.size()). But we can just refer to \old(this.size()).

Thus: assert (index >= 0 && index < \old(this.size())) => \forall int i; index < i && i < this.size(); this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i)));

